            <ArticleTitle>Structure of life frustrations in subjects prone to ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Men, exhibiting risk factors of ischaemic heart disease (hypertension, family history, smoking, diabetes, retinal angiopathy, hypercholesterolaemia) reported to be less frustrated practically in all spheres of life than non-risk men. In women the overall difference was less conspicuous but the structure of frustrations somewhat differed. The IHD-prone women were more frustrated in the sphere of material needs and of assessment of their own health, which suggests that in them a certain feeling of illness is yet developing. On the other hand in the sphere of work and in their interpersonal relations they were less frustrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
